  data: {
    LLM: "Learn the card values and marianna combinations. Try to capture Aces and Tens (brisques) in tricks. Declare mariannas when you have them.\n\nSince both players can declare combinations in any trick, there's no particular incentive to win tricks unless they contain valuable cards - except for the very last trick worth 10 extra points. In opening tricks, get rid of useless cards (7, 8, 9 of non-trump suits) and aim to collect combinations. When your hand consists only of 'useful' cards (brisques, kings, queens, jacks, low trumps), choose between trying to win tricks or declaring more combinations.\n\nThe holder of the 7 of trumps should always exchange it, but wait until ready to use the trump indicator card. Remember played cards - once a king or queen has been played, no further mariannas are possible in that suit. Use the tactic of 'fare morire in mano una marianna' - acting as though you have a marianna to discourage opponents from declaring theirs.",
    Player: "Learn the card values and marianna combinations. Try to capture Aces and Tens (brisques) in tricks. Declare mariannas when you have them.\n\nSince both players can declare combinations in any trick, there's no particular incentive to win tricks unless they contain valuable cards - except for the very last trick worth 10 extra points. In opening tricks, get rid of useless cards (7, 8, 9 of non-trump suits) and aim to collect combinations. When your hand consists only of 'useful' cards (brisques, kings, queens, jacks, low trumps), choose between trying to win tricks or declaring more combinations.\n\nThe holder of the 7 of trumps should always exchange it, but wait until ready to use the trump indicator card. Remember played cards - once a king or queen has been played, no further mariannas are possible in that suit. Use the tactic of 'fare morire in mano una marianna' - acting as though you have a marianna to discourage opponents from declaring theirs.",
